1. What is the primary purpose of an Operating System?

A) Compile Programs
B) Manage Hardware and Software Resources
C) Design Software
D) Create Databases

✅ Answer: B

Why?
OS acts as an interface between user and hardware and manages CPU, memory, files, and devices.

2. Which is NOT an Operating System?

A) Linux
B) Windows
C) Oracle
D) macOS

✅ Answer: C

Why?
Oracle is primarily a Database Management System (DBMS).

3. Which component manages the CPU?

A) File Manager
B) Process Manager
C) Device Driver
D) Shell

✅ Answer: B

Why?
Process Management allocates CPU to processes.

4. Which scheduling algorithm follows FIFO?

A) FCFS
B) SJF
C) Round Robin
D) Priority

✅ Answer: A

Why?
FCFS = First Come First Serve.

5. What is the brain of the OS?

A) Kernel
B) Shell
C) Compiler
D) Driver

✅ Answer: A

Why?
Kernel controls all major OS operations.

6. Which memory is volatile?

A) SSD
B) HDD
C) RAM
D) ROM

✅ Answer: C

Why?
RAM loses data when power is off.

7. Which memory is non-volatile?

A) Cache
B) RAM
C) Registers
D) ROM

✅ Answer: D

Why?
ROM retains data even after power loss.

8. Which OS allows multiple users?

A) MS-DOS
B) Linux
C) Palm OS
D) None

✅ Answer: B

Why?
Linux supports multiple users simultaneously.

9. What is a Process?

A) Program in Execution
B) File in Memory
C) Program in Disk
D) Hardware Unit

✅ Answer: A

Why?
A process is an actively running program.

10. What is PCB?

A) Program Control Block
B) Process Control Block
C) Processor Control Board
D) Program Configuration Block

✅ Answer: B

Why?
PCB stores information about a process.

11. Which scheduling algorithm gives minimum average waiting time?

A) FCFS
B) Priority
C) SJF
D) RR

✅ Answer: C

Why?
Shortest Job First minimizes waiting time mathematically.

12. Round Robin scheduling is designed for:

A) Batch Systems
B) Real-Time Systems
C) Time Sharing Systems
D) Multiprocessing

✅ Answer: C

Why?
Each process gets a fixed time quantum.

13. Context Switching occurs when:

A) Process changes CPU state
B) File opens
C) Disk reads
D) OS boots

✅ Answer: A

Why?
CPU switches from one process to another.

14. Which scheduler selects process from Ready Queue?

A) Long-Term
B) Medium-Term
C) Short-Term
D) None

✅ Answer: C

Why?
CPU Scheduler chooses next process.

15. What is Deadlock?

A) Infinite Loop
B) CPU Crash
C) Processes waiting forever for resources
D) Memory Overflow

✅ Answer: C

Why?
Processes block each other permanently.

16. Deadlock requires how many conditions?

A) 2
B) 3
C) 4
D) 5

✅ Answer: C

Why?
Mutual Exclusion, Hold & Wait, No Preemption, Circular Wait.

17. Which condition is NOT necessary for deadlock?

A) Circular Wait
B) Mutual Exclusion
C) Time Sharing
D) Hold and Wait

✅ Answer: C

Why?
Time sharing has no relation to deadlock.

18. Banker’s Algorithm is used for:

A) Scheduling
B) Deadlock Avoidance
C) Paging
D) File Management

✅ Answer: B

Why?
It checks safe state before allocating resources.

19. Semaphore is used for:

A) Scheduling
B) Synchronization
C) Paging
D) Booting

✅ Answer: B

Why?
Semaphores prevent race conditions.

20. Race Condition occurs when:

A) One process executes
B) Multiple processes access shared data simultaneously
C) OS crashes
D) Memory full

✅ Answer: B

Why?
Outcome depends on execution order.

21. Binary Semaphore values are:

A) 0 and 1
B) 1 and 2
C) 2 and 3
D) Any integer

✅ Answer: A

Why?
Works like a lock.

22. Mutex stands for:

A) Mutual Exclusion
B) Multiple Exclusion
C) Memory Utility
D) None

✅ Answer: A

23. Which memory is fastest?

A) HDD
B) SSD
C) RAM
D) Register

✅ Answer: D

Why?
Registers are inside CPU.

24. Virtual Memory uses:

A) Cache
B) Secondary Storage
C) Registers
D) ROM

✅ Answer: B

25. Paging eliminates:

A) External Fragmentation
B) Internal Fragmentation
C) Deadlock
D) Scheduling

✅ Answer: A

26. Fixed-size blocks in memory are called:

A) Segments
B) Pages
C) Frames
D) Partitions

✅ Answer: B

27. Physical memory is divided into:

A) Pages
B) Segments
C) Frames
D) Blocks

✅ Answer: C

28. What is Thrashing?

A) Excessive Paging
B) CPU Overload
C) Deadlock
D) Boot Failure

✅ Answer: A

29. Page Fault occurs when:

A) CPU Busy
B) Page not found in RAM
C) Disk Error
D) OS Failure

✅ Answer: B

30. FIFO Page Replacement removes:

A) Oldest Page
B) Newest Page
C) Random Page
D) Largest Page

✅ Answer: A

31. LRU stands for?

A) Least Recently Used
B) Last Removed Unit
C) Least Required Unit
D) Last Required Use

✅ Answer: A

32. Which page replacement is generally better?

A) FIFO
B) LRU
C) Random
D) FCFS

✅ Answer: B

33. Segmentation supports:

A) Logical Memory View
B) Physical Memory View
C) Scheduling
D) Paging Only

✅ Answer: A

34. Internal Fragmentation occurs in:

A) Paging
B) Segmentation
C) Deadlock
D) Scheduling

✅ Answer: A

35. What is a File?

A) Collection of Data
B) CPU Unit
C) Memory Block
D) Process

✅ Answer: A

36. Which file allocation method uses linked list?

A) Contiguous
B) Linked
C) Indexed
D) Paging

✅ Answer: B

37. FAT stands for:

A) File Allocation Table
B) File Access Tool
C) Fast Access Table
D) Fast Allocation Tool

✅ Answer: A

38. NTFS belongs to:

A) Linux
B) Windows
C) Android
D) UNIX

✅ Answer: B

39. In UNIX everything is treated as:

A) Process
B) Thread
C) File
D) Memory

✅ Answer: C

40. Which command shows current directory in Linux?

A) ls
B) pwd
C) cd
D) dir

✅ Answer: B

41. Linux kernel is an example of:

A) Microkernel
B) Hybrid Kernel
C) Monolithic Kernel
D) Exokernel

✅ Answer: C) Monolithic Kernel

Why?
Linux keeps most OS services inside the kernel space for performance.

42. Windows kernel is generally classified as:

A) Monolithic
B) Hybrid
C) Microkernel
D) Exokernel

✅ Answer: B) Hybrid

Why?
Windows combines features of monolithic and microkernel architectures.

43. A daemon process is:

A) Foreground Process
B) Background Service Process
C) User Process
D) Zombie Process

✅ Answer: B) Background Service Process

Why?
Daemons run in the background and provide services like printing, networking, etc.

44. The fork() system call creates:

A) Thread
B) Child Process
C) Interrupt
D) File

✅ Answer: B) Child Process

Why?
fork() duplicates the calling process.

45. The exec() system call is used to:

A) Create Process
B) Delete Process
C) Replace Current Process Image with New Program
D) Create Thread

✅ Answer: C

Why?
exec() loads and runs a new program in the current process.

46. A Zombie Process is:

A) Running Process
B) Waiting Process
C) Terminated Process whose PCB still exists
D) New Process

✅ Answer: C

Why?
The process has ended, but the parent has not yet collected its exit status.

47. An Orphan Process is:

A) Process without Memory
B) Child Process whose Parent has Terminated
C) Zombie Process
D) Ready Process

✅ Answer: B

Why?
Its parent dies before the child finishes.

48. System Call Interface acts as:

A) CPU Scheduler
B) User-Kernel Bridge
C) Memory Manager
D) Compiler

✅ Answer: B

Why?
It allows user programs to request OS services.

49. A Trap is:

A) Hardware Interrupt
B) Software Interrupt
C) Scheduler
D) Memory Block

✅ Answer: B

Why?
A trap is generated intentionally by software.

50. Interrupts can be generated by:

A) Hardware Only
B) Software Only
C) Hardware and Software Both
D) CPU Only

✅ Answer: C

Why?
Keyboard → Hardware interrupt, System Call → Software interrupt.

51. Dispatcher is responsible for:

A) Memory Allocation
B) Process Creation
C) Giving CPU Control to Selected Process
D) File Allocation

✅ Answer: C

Why?
Dispatcher performs context switch and transfers CPU.

52. Ready Queue contains:

A) Running Processes
B) Blocked Processes
C) Ready-to-Run Processes
D) Terminated Processes

✅ Answer: C

53. Degree of Multiprogramming means:

A) Number of CPUs
B) Number of Processes in Memory
C) Number of Users
D) Number of Files

✅ Answer: B

54. Spooling stands for:

A) Simultaneous Peripheral Operations On-Line
B) System Peripheral Operations Online Logic
C) Shared Peripheral Output Logic
D) Sequential Processing Online Logic

✅ Answer: A

Why?
Jobs are stored in a buffer before execution.

55. DMA stands for:

A) Direct Memory Access
B) Data Memory Allocation
C) Dynamic Memory Access
D) Direct Machine Access

✅ Answer: A

56. During booting, what is loaded into memory?

A) Application Software
B) Kernel
C) Browser
D) Compiler

✅ Answer: B

57. Cold Boot means:

A) Restarting Computer
B) Booting from Powered-Off State
C) Sleep Mode
D) Hibernate Mode

✅ Answer: B

58. Warm Boot means:

A) First Start
B) Restart/Reboot without Power Off
C) Shutdown
D) Sleep

✅ Answer: B

59. Shell is:

A) Hardware Device
B) Command Interpreter
C) Process Scheduler
D) Memory Manager

✅ Answer: B

60. CLI stands for:

A) Common Language Interface
B) Command Line Interface
C) Computer Logic Interface
D) Central Line Interface

✅ Answer: B

61. GUI stands for:

A) General User Interface
B) Graphical User Interface
C) Graphic Utility Interface
D) General Utility Interface

✅ Answer: B) Graphical User Interface

Why?
GUI allows users to interact through windows, icons, menus, and pointers instead of typing commands.

62. Time Quantum is used in:

A) FCFS
B) SJF
C) Round Robin
D) Priority Scheduling

✅ Answer: C) Round Robin

Why?
Each process gets a fixed CPU time called a time quantum.

63. Starvation is most common in:

A) FCFS
B) Round Robin
C) Priority Scheduling
D) FIFO

✅ Answer: C) Priority Scheduling

Why?
Low-priority processes may wait indefinitely if higher-priority processes keep arriving.

64. Aging is used to solve:

A) Deadlock
B) Thrashing
C) Starvation
D) Fragmentation

✅ Answer: C) Starvation

Why?
The waiting process's priority is gradually increased.

65. A Thread is:

A) Heavyweight Process
B) Lightweight Process
C) File
D) Memory Unit

✅ Answer: B) Lightweight Process

Why?
Threads share resources of a process and are cheaper to create.

66. Multithreading means:

A) Multiple CPUs
B) Multiple Processes
C) Multiple Threads within a Process
D) Multiple Kernels

✅ Answer: C

67. IPC stands for:

A) Internal Process Communication
B) Inter Process Communication
C) Inter Program Control
D) Internal Program Control

✅ Answer: B

Why?
IPC enables processes to exchange data.

68. Which is an IPC mechanism?

A) Pipe
B) Semaphore
C) Shared Memory
D) All of These

✅ Answer: D

69. Fastest IPC mechanism is:

A) Pipe
B) Message Queue
C) Shared Memory
D) Socket

✅ Answer: C

Why?
Processes directly access the same memory region.

70. Message Passing is:

A) CPU Scheduling
B) Memory Management
C) IPC Method
D) Deadlock Prevention

✅ Answer: C

71. Cache Memory is located:

A) Inside/Very Near CPU
B) Hard Disk
C) SSD
D) Network

✅ Answer: A

Why?
Cache stores frequently used data for faster access.

72. Swap Space is:

A) CPU Area
